Package: RedKinNet
Title: Selection of Unrelated Individuals from Kinship Networks
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Paolo", "Dalena", , "paolodalena97@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2920-9572"))
Description: Selects sets of mutually unrelated individuals from pairwise
    kinship estimates. Pairs related above a kinship threshold, such as the
    cutoffs of Manichaikul et al. (2010) <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btq559>,
    form a network whose connected components (families) are resolved as
    maximum independent set problems, by structural rules and an exact
    elimination algorithm that also handles the large families of genetic
    isolates. A largest set of unrelated individuals can be drawn at random,
    uniformly among all such sets with exact inclusion probabilities, chosen
    within families by preferences for individuals, or chosen jointly across
    families to approach a target proportion or mean of a covariate,
    optionally trading selection size for composition. Samples are screened
    for duplicates and possible contamination, and diagnostics document how
    each individual was selected.
